\section*{Theoretical framework}

Our framework, which integrates neural network potential and polarizable long-range interactions, is depicted in Fig. 1. For a given chemical system and boundary conditions, our goal is to construct a mapping from atomic coordinates \(\mathbf{r}_{i}\) and atomic types \(Z_{i}\) to the total potential energy \(E_{\mathrm{pot}}\). The potential energy is expressed as the sum of the second-order expansion \({ }^{30}\) with respect to charge fluctuations and the density functional theory \({ }^{39}\) D3 (DFT-D3) van der Waals dispersion energies correction
